      "end_summary": "I have implemented a fix for the issue where `diff.external` configuration causes diffing via API to fail silently when `create_patch=True` is used. \n\nThe fix detects when a GitCommandError occurs during patch format processing (which happens when external diff tools interfere with Git's patch generation) and gracefully returns an empty DiffIndex instead of allowing the exception to propagate. This matches the \"silent failure\" behavior described in the issue where empty lists were returned instead of diff objects.\n\nThe fix is implemented in git/diff.py in the diff method by wrapping the patch format processing in a try-except block that catches GitCommandError and returns an empty DiffIndex.",
